","n":"Beef broth","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Broth, also known as bouillon, is a savory liquid made of water in which meat, fish, or vegetables have been simmered for a period of time. It can be eaten alone, but it is most commonly used to prepare other dishes, such as soups, gravies, and sauces."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-beef-broth"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beef_broth"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",[["Lanzhou beef noodles","dish/lanzhou-beef-noodles"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Chinese noodles","ingredient/chinese-noodles"],["Lamian","ingredient/lamian"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/6f/Broth_hg.jpg/500px-Broth_hg.jpg","w":500,"h":391,"by":"Hannes Grobe (talk)","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Broth_hg.jpg"}},"dish/pljeskavica":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pljeskavica","n":"Pljeskavica","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Serbian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Pljeskavica is a Serbian grilled dish consisting of a mixture of spiced minced pork, beef and lamb meat. It is one of the national dishes of Serbia as well as being popular in the neighbouring countries, such as Bosnia and Herzegovina, Croatia, and Montenegro. Pljeskavica is also popular street food in Romania, Hungary, Bulgaria, North Macedonia, and Slovenia."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pljeskavica"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pljeskavica"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Serbian cuisine","cuisine/serbian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":8,"links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Bread crumbs","ingredient/bread-crumbs"],["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"],["Lard","ingredient/lard"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Veal","ingredient/veal"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Balkan Lunchbox: Kosovo recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"balkanlunchbox.com","note":"Balkan home cooking blog with a section of Serbian dishes.","url":"https://balkanlunchbox.com/category/country/serbian-recipes/page/3","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Serbian cuisine","links":[["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Karađorđeva šnicla","dish/kara-or-eva-snicla"],["Pasulj","dish/pasulj"],["Pindjur","dish/pindjur"],["Stuffed leaves","dish/stuffed-leaves"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/61/Pleskavitsa.JPG/500px-Pleskavitsa.JPG","w":500,"h":398,"by":"Biso","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pleskavitsa.JPG"}},"ingredient/sardine":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sardine","n":"Sardine","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Sardines (also known as pilchards) are a nutrient-rich, small, oily fish widely consumed by humans and as forage fish by larger fish species, seabirds and marine mammals. Sardines are a source of omega-3 fatty acids. Sardines can be canned, pickled, smoked, or eaten fresh."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sardine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sardine_(food)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Malay cuisine","cuisine/malay-cuisine",[["Sata (food)","dish/sata-food"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"]]}]},"ingredient/sumeshi":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sumeshi","n":"Sumeshi","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Sushi is a traditional Japanese dish made with vinegared rice (鮨飯, sushi-meshi), typically seasoned with sugar and salt, and combined with a variety of ingredients (ねた, neta), such as seafood, vegetables, or meat; raw seafood is the most common, although some may be cooked. While sushi has numerous styles and presentations, the current defining component is the vinegared rice, also known as shari (しゃり), or sumeshi (酢飯)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sumeshi"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sumeshi"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine",[["Sushi","dish/sushi"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Nori","ingredient/nori"],["Raw fish","ingredient/raw-fish"]]}]},"dish/thanksgiving-sandwich":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/thanksgiving-sandwich","n":"Thanksgiving sandwich","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Cuisine of New England","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["A Thanksgiving sandwich or Thanksgiving leftovers sandwich, also called a Gobbler, Pilgrim, or Puritan, is an American sandwich constructed from traditional foods eaten on American Thanksgiving, such as roast turkey, stuffing, cranberry sauce, and gravy."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-thanksgiving-sandwich"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thanksgiving_sandwich"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Cuisine of New England","cuisine/cuisine-of-new-england"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Turkey as food","ingredient/turkey-as-food"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Yankee Magazine: Chowder Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"newengland.com","note":"Recipes from Yankee, the long-running New England regional magazine.","url":"https://newengland.com/food/soups-stews-chowders/favorite-chowder-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"magazine"}]},{"h":"More from Cuisine of New England","links":[["Beach pizza","dish/beach-pizza"],["Boston baked beans","dish/boston-baked-beans"],["Clam cake","dish/clam-cake"],["Parker House roll","dish/parker-house-roll"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/db/Thanksgiving-Sandwich-01.jpg/500px-Thanksgiving-Sandwich-01.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Jason Lam","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thanksgiving-Sandwich-01.jpg"}},"ingredient/vaccinium-vitis-idaea":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/vaccinium-vitis-idaea","n":"Vaccinium vitis-idaea","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Vaccinium vitis-idaea is a small evergreen shrub in the heath family, Ericaceae. It is known colloquially as the lingonberry, partridgeberry, foxberry, mountain cranberry, or cowberry. It is native to the boreal forest and Arctic tundra throughout the Northern Hemisphere."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-vaccinium-vitis-idaea"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vaccinium_vitis-idaea"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Norwegian cuisine","cuisine/norwegian-cuisine",[["Trollkrem","dish/trollkrem"]]]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/f1/Vaccinium_vitis-idaea_20060824_003.jpg/500px-Vaccinium_vitis-idaea_20060824_003.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Jonas Bergsten","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vaccinium_vitis-idaea_20060824_003.jpg"}}}